a new chapter for the Raja Park says  Gautama Rajapaksa brother of a former  president and himself an ex defense  secretary  now the candidate for the Sri Lanka pada  juniperus Munna party for elections  expected later this year I love my  country I'm proud of my country and I  have a vision for the future of this  country I value this opportunity to give  leadership to all Sri Lankans and bring  peace happiness and prosperity to the  motherland  Gautama Rajapaksa led the military to  victory over the Tamil Tigers ending 26  years of civil war he was given a free  hand by his brother then President  Mahinda Rajapaksa to do so but  accusations of human rights abuses and  war crimes plagued his tenure many  Tamils in the north and east are still  looking for answers about their missing  relatives or those abducted under Raja  Parks's watch some complain of  intimidation and harassment when they  tried to speak up Sharon Saviour who has  worked with these communities says his  candidacy for president is causing  concern he's seen as a terminator on  dissent yes so in that contact like an  old people are a bit worried about I  mean in any kind of dissent will not be  tolerated so this this space maybe there  were like you know a little bit of space  for not just alone the civil society  members but as public in general in the  north and east or like areas where the  numerical minority is a living so in  that context that space whether that is  going to shrink Rajapaksa seems to be  aware of such concerns telling the party  convention on sunday that the diversity  of communities in sri lanka  is its strength it's taken one term for  Sri Lankans who voted a Rajapaksa  president out of office to look at his  brother as a potential leader the reason  according to one political commentator  lies with the current government which  has not fulfilled people's expectations  the failure of the democratic experiment  has opened up space new political space  for and the counter Democratic  authoritarian alternative so whatever  our personal personifies you know that  you know political space which has been  opened up in Sri Lankan society the new  candidate gave supporters some insights  into his views on the country's  sovereignity security and the  environment presidential elections must  be held by December 8th those  campaigning for gota BAE Rajapaksa say  he's a terminator and will stamp out  corruption and fraud but won't be an  authoritarian leader that something Sri  Lankan voters will have to decide  whether to believe or not when they  choose their next president Meena  Fernandez al Jazeera Colombo
 

